---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import config from "../../site.config.ts";
import { CONSENT_TEXT } from "@uaeprop/site-kit";

const title = "Privacy | Handover";
const description =
  "What Handover collects, why, how long it is kept, and how to have it deleted.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="shell py-12 md:py-16">
    <p class="label mb-4">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-[16ch] text-[clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3rem)]">What we collect and why</h1>
    <p class="measure mt-6 text-[1.1rem] text-ink-2">
      Short version: nothing unless you send it. This page has no account, no login,
      and no advertising trackers.
    </p>

    <div class="measure mt-10 space-y-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">If you send us a message</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          We store the name, email address, phone number and message you submit, together
          with the page you sent it from, the date and time, your IP address and browser
          user agent. The IP and user agent are kept because they are how we demonstrate
          that consent was genuinely given, and how we detect automated abuse.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink-2">
          We also store the exact wording of the consent you agreed to, which at the time
          of writing reads: &ldquo;{CONSENT_TEXT}&rdquo;
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">Who it is shared with</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          If you ask to be introduced to a broker, we pass your name, contact details and
          the substance of your enquiry to a licensed UAE real estate brokerage. That is
          the point of the introduction and it is what you consent to when you submit the
          form. We may be paid by that brokerage for the introduction.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink-2">
          We do not sell your details to list brokers, marketing databases, or anyone else.
          A single introduction is not a licence for us to keep distributing your details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">Processors we use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          Your submission is stored in a managed Postgres database and delivered to us by
          email through a transactional email provider. Form submissions are screened by
          Cloudflare Turnstile to block automated abuse. Each of these providers processes
          the data only to deliver that specific function.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">Analytics</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          If you consent, we use Google Analytics to count visits and Microsoft Clarity to
          see which parts of the guide people actually read. Both are loaded only after you
          opt in &mdash; decline, and neither is ever requested. Neither is used for
          advertising or to build a profile of you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          Enquiries are deleted 24 months after they are submitted. If you want yours
          removed sooner, email
          <a href={`mailto:${config.contact.email}`}>{config.contact.email}</a> and we will
          delete it. You do not have to give a reason, and we will confirm when it is done.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          Under the UAE Personal Data Protection Law you can ask what we hold about you,
          ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and withdraw consent at any time.
          Withdrawing consent does not undo an introduction already made, but it stops any
          further contact from us. Use the email address above for any of these.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-[1.35rem]">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          If this policy changes materially we will update the consent wording and its
          version, so records remain interpretable against the terms that applied when they
          were collected.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
